  "summaries": {
    "en": "Scadutree Fragment routing, boss pattern decomposition, and risk-managed punish plans for the Shadow Realm. Covers Messmer, Romina, and Promised Consort Radahn.",
    "ja": "影の地のスカデューツリーの欠片収集ルート、ボス行動分解、低リスク反撃プランを網羅。メスメル・ロミナ・約束された星の時代ラダーンを収録。"
  },
  "category": "soulslike",
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552820728-8b83bb6b773f?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Scadutree Fragments grant a DLC-specific damage bonus and damage reduction that scales non-linearly—collecting the first 10 fragments provides roughly 40% of the total benefit. Complete Castle Ensis before any DLC boss.",
      "Block count determines punish window length more than attack animation speed. Identify whether a move ends on the left or right side of the boss model—punish to the opposite side to minimise the chance of catching a turn-attack.",
      "Stamina management is stricter than base game: DLC bosses deal 20–35% more poise damage per hit. Maintain a 40% stamina buffer before blocking sequences; exhaust under 25% and you risk a guard break into a punish string.",
      "Most DLC bosses have a stance-break threshold 30–40% higher than base game equivalents. Use stance-break tools (Claw Talisman jump attacks, charged R2) at phase transitions when stance meters reset, not during open-field trading.",
      "Positioning resets over trading: when uncertain about an attack's hitbox, immediately reposition to neutral rather than rolling into the attack. Most DLC attacks have deceptive tracking arcs that punish reactive dodge timing."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "欠片のスカデューツリーはDLC専用のダメージ加算・軽減を非線形で与える。最初の10個で恩恵の約40%を得られる。城エニスを制覇してから各DLCボスに挑む。",
      "確定反撃ウィンドウはガード回数より攻撃アニメーション速度で決まる。攻撃がボスモデルの左右どちらで終わるかを確認し、反対側を攻撃してターン攻撃に巻き込まれないようにする。",
      "スタミナ管理は本編より厳しい。DLCボスのガード削りは1ヒット当たり20〜35%多い。ブロック連続前にスタミナ40%以上を維持し、25%以下でのガードはガード崩し→追撃リスクがある。",
      "多くのDLCボスのスタンス破壊閾値は本編相当ボスより30〜40%高い。スタンス破壊手段（爪タリスマン+ジャンプ攻撃、溜めR2）はフィールドでの打ち合いより、フェーズ移行時のメーターリセット直後に使う。",
      "不確実な攻撃はトレードせずに位置リセットを優先する。DLCの多くの攻撃はリアクティブな回避タイミングを逆手に取る追尾弧を持つ。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Entry Route: Scadutree Fragment Priority",
        "body": "Upon entering the Shadow Realm via the Miquella Cocoon, immediately route to Castle Ensis to collect the first 5 Scadutree Fragments without engaging a major boss. Follow the path: Belurat Tower Settlement (fragments 1–3) → Castle Ensis outer walls (fragments 4–5). This baseline gives enough stat scaling to make Messmer's first phase survivable. Attempting Messmer before fragment 5 results in one-shot deaths from his fire pillar combo on most standard builds."
      },
      {
        "title": "Reading Messmer the Impaler",
        "body": "Messmer has two distinct attack categories: spear thrust sequences (safe to dodge forward-through) and fire explosion combos (must dodge backward, not sideways). His phase transition triggers a spear slam with 180° tracking—do not dodge the slam; instead run laterally 3 full steps. The safest punish window in phase 1 is after his double-thrust end lag (1.8 seconds). In phase 2, target punishes exclusively after his snake explosion animation fully settles (serpent model disappears completely)."
      },
      {
        "title": "Shadow Realm Early Navigation",
        "body": "The Gravesite Plain is the central hub; unlock all four cardinal Grace points before pushing forward. The northern route (Scadu Altus via the fort) and southern route (Belurat via the river) both merge at the Shadow Keep. Taking the northern route first gives access to the Moorth Ruins fragment cluster and a +7 Scadutree Blessing before the Shadow Keep, which is the recommended pre-Messmer checkpoint."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Romina, Saint of the Bud",
        "body": "Romina is weak to fire damage and her scarlet rot aura can be countered with Preserving Boluses (carry 10). Her centipede body has a hitbox that tracks player position on the ground but not in the air—jump attacks from Claw Talisman builds deal consistent damage while avoiding the rot aura radius. Her second phase adds a chrysalis charge attack; the safe dodge window is after the third wing beat, not the first or second (both are feints)."
      },
      {
        "title": "Bayle the Dread",
        "body": "Bayle is the hardest optional boss in the DLC. He has three attacks with identical wind-ups but different execution: wing slam, bite, and tail sweep. Differentiate them by hip position: raised hip predicts tail sweep, lowered hip predicts bite or wing slam. Stance breaks are exceptionally effective against Bayle—use Claw Talisman jump heavy attacks from behind when his wing slam animation ends. Two full stance breaks in phase 1 effectively double punish windows."
      },
      {
        "title": "Scadutree Blessing Mid-Route",
        "body": "After Shadow Keep, the fragment clusters shift to the Rauh Base and Ancient Ruins zones. Route Rauh before Ancient Ruins: the dense fragment clustering in Rauh (11 fragments across 4 sites) versus Ancient Ruins (6 fragments across 7 sites) makes Rauh far more time-efficient per fragment. Reaching Scadutree Blessing +10 before the final area makes the Promised Consort Radahn significantly more forgiving."
      },
      {
        "title": "Spirit Ash Selection for DLC",
        "body": "Black Knife Tiche (Ashes of War: Ash of War or standalone summon) remains the most effective Spirit Ash for DLC bosses due to her dodge pattern matching DLC attack timings. Mimic Tear performs inconsistently against fire-damage bosses (Messmer, Bayle) because it attempts to block rather than dodge. Ancient Dragon Knight Kristoff provides useful poise interrupt loops but requires 8 Memory Stones to use effectively alongside a main weapon buff."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Promised Consort Radahn: Phase 1",
        "body": "Radahn's phase 1 is a gravitational sword combo boss. His most dangerous move is the delayed overhead slam—the safest response is a full-sprint roll toward his left hip, not a panic-timed dodge. Punish windows are 2–3 hits maximum after any single attack. Do not extend past 3 hits even when his animation appears to have more end lag—the gravitational pull interrupt can catch greedy combos with guaranteed counter damage."
      },
      {
        "title": "Promised Consort Radahn: Phase 2",
        "body": "Phase 2 triggers at 50% HP with a cinematic that adds Miquella passive AI. Miquella grabs Radahn mid-attack to create brief stagger windows—these are bonus punish frames, not the primary punish cycle. The key change in phase 2 is a new cross-slash that tracks laterally; dodge toward Radahn's waist rather than away to pass through the hitbox. Healing is safest after the celestial shower attack fully ends (all light pillars disappear)."
      },
      {
        "title": "Final Build Checklist",
        "body": "For any build at Scadutree +12 or higher: equip Shard of Alexander (+15% charged attack damage), Two Fingers Heirloom (+5 Faith for incantation scaling), and Dragoncrest Greatshield Talisman (−20% physical damage taken). These three talismans cover the widest spectrum of DLC boss damage types. Replace Dragoncrest with Claw Talisman for stance-heavy melee approaches against Bayle or Romina specifically."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Panic rolling into delayed attacks—Messmer's spear explosion and Radahn's cross-slash both have deliberate delay timing specifically to punish reactive roll inputs. Commit to either forward-through or full sprint instead.",
      "Trying to heal without creating a sight-line break—healing animation in Elden Ring is 1.4 seconds; without moving behind a pillar or around a corner, most DLC bosses can close the distance in under 0.8 seconds.",
      "Entering Shadow Realm with fewer than 5 Scadutree Fragments—the defensive scaling provided by the first 5 fragments reduces incoming damage by approximately 30%, which is the difference between surviving combo strings and dying to them.",
      "Using all Physick flasks before the phase transition—always keep one Crystal Tear Physick active entering any phase 2. The DLC phase transitions are sudden and the opening animation is an intentional window to chug, but only if a flask remains.",
      "Spending Remembrance Items too early—Messmer's Remembrance can be duplicated at the Mausoleum and provides two unique weapons and a sorcery. Duplicate before spending; the Mausoleum is accessible before the final boss."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "遅延攻撃に焦って回避入力する。メスメルの槍爆発とラダーンのクロス斬りは、リアクティブ回避を逆手に取る意図的な遅延タイミングを持つ。前方抜けか全力疾走に切り替える。",
      "視線切りなしで回復を試みる。エルデンリングの飲み動作は1.4秒。柱や壁の陰に移動しないと多くのDLCボスは0.8秒未満で間合いを詰めてくる。",
      "欠片のスカデューツリー5個未満で影の地に入る。最初の5個で受けるダメージが約30%減少し、コンボを生き延びられるかどうかの境界になる。",
      "フェーズ移行前に聖杯瓶を全て使い切る。DLCのフェーズ移行は突然で、移行演出が意図的な補充窓口になっているが、瓶が残っている場合のみ有効。",
      "記念品を早期に消費する。メスメルの記念品は霊廟で複製でき、固有武器2種とソーサリーが手に入る。最終ボス前に必ず複製する。"
    ]
  },
